 verified, and graceful, with no escalation history.","signal_handler":"Install before pre-acquire checks and guard acquisition. SIGTERM before acquisition records a pre-acquire failure without claiming consumption. Block SIGTERM only over guard mutation/handoff with pthread_sigmask, mark the acquired state before unblocking, then route any pending signal into consumed FAIL handling. During campaign SIGTERM raises RUNNER_INTERRUPTED_BY_SIGNAL:SIGTERM; during teardown/finalization it latches without throwing, forces FAIL resynchronization through handler restoration, and the previous handler is restored exactly once."}}